sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant K as Kernel launch
    participant GS as Gigathread engine
    participant SM as SM
    participant Reg as Register file
    participant L1 as L1 / shared memory
    participant L2 as L2 cache
    participant HBM as HBM
    K->>GS: grid of thread blocks
    GS->>SM: assign a block to an SM with free resources
    SM->>Reg: allocate registers per thread
    Note over Reg: register pressure caps how many warps fit — that is occupancy
    SM->>L1: threads in a block share this
    SM->>L2: miss goes here
    L2->>HBM: miss goes here
    Note over L1,HBM: each step down is roughly an order of magnitude slower
    SM->>SM: tensor cores handle the matrix multiplies
